(BRANDGUARD GLOBAL MARKETING AND BRAND COMPLIANCE GUIDELINES \(2026\)) '
(Section 1: General Tone and Voice Requirements) '
(All official marketing content, social media posts, and advertising materials must maintain an authoritative, professional, and respectful tone.) '
(Aggressive urgency language, hype claims, and deceptive clickbait tactics are strictly prohibited across all brand channels.) '
T*
(Section 2: Claims, Guarantees, and Performance Statements) '
(Policy 2.1: Absolute Guarantees Prohibited.) '
(Marketing content must not contain absolute outcome guarantees or promise 100% results. We never use phrases such as 'guarantees 100% results', 'never fails', or 'zero risk'. Outcomes must be qualified based on customer use cases.) '
(Policy 2.2: Superlative and Market Leadership Claims.) '
(Do not claim a product is the best in the world or #1 in the market without verified, accredited third-party audit documentation. Statements such as 'best solution in the world' or 'superior to all alternatives' are prohibited unless explicitly authorized by Legal.) '
T*
(Section 3: Regulated Sector Disclaimers and Prohibited Terms) '
(Policy 3.1: Medical and Health Claims.) '
(Avoid unapproved medical or clinical claims. The company does not offer medical cures, and words such as 'miracle cure', 'eliminates disease', or 'clinically proven cure' are strictly forbidden.) '
(Policy 3.2: Financial Promises.) '
(Financial outcomes, get-rich assertions, and guaranteed returns are strictly prohibited.) '
(Policy 3.3: Mandatory Disclaimers.) '
(All promotional offers and metric outcomes must display the standard disclosure: 'Terms and conditions apply. Results may vary.') '
T*
ET

